package: Hover Preview
author: Seth Rosenthal
organization: OpenUTV
version: 1.0
rv: 3.12.10
openrv: 1.0.0
requires: ''

modes:
  - file: hover_preview_mode
    load: immediate

description: |

  <p>
  Shows a preview of the frame under the mouse when you hover over the
  timeline: a small picture of that frame with its source name, in a panel
  just above the timeline that points at the frame.
  </p>

  <p>
  The View menu gets a "Hover Preview" submenu to choose when the preview
  appears: Off, When Paused (the default) or Always. The choice is stored
  in the preferences, so it is remembered when you exit.
  </p>

  <h2>How It Works</h2>

  <p>
  The mode watches pointer events over the timeline and asks the timeline
  which frame is under the mouse. It sends the internal event
  "hover-preview-show" with "frame|x|y|label" (x and y are where the
  panel's arrow points, in framebuffer pixels) and "hover-preview-clear"
  when the preview should go away. UTV renders the frame and draws the
  panel. The mode passes every event on, so the timeline and other modes
  still receive them.
  </p>
